Subject: [PATCH] nfnetlink: keep receiving events after a socket overrun

Netlink reports a receive queue overrun through EPOLLERR. Without
ULOOP_ERROR_CB, uloop removes the socket from epoll before handle_event()
can consume the error. Periodic dumps keep running, but event delivery
never resumes. Leave the socket registered so subsequent reads can drain
the queue after nl_recv() consumes the error.

--- a/nfnetlink.c
+++ b/nfnetlink.c
@@ -395,7 +395,7 @@ nfnetlink_connect(int bufsize)
 	ufd.cb = handle_event;
 	ufd.fd = nl_socket_get_fd(nl);
 
-	if (uloop_fd_add(&ufd, ULOOP_READ))
+	if (uloop_fd_add(&ufd, ULOOP_READ | ULOOP_ERROR_CB))
 		return -errno;
 
 	return 0;
